# Rectangular editing: DECERA, DECSERA, DECFRA and DECCRA (the area as CSI Pt ; Pl ; Pb ; Pr).
#
# The cases run on an eight by eight screen filled with 64 different characters, so that a cell
# shows where it came from. An area counts from the screen's corner, or from the scrolling
# region's with origin mode, and is cut to the screen; the margins do not limit it and the cursor
# does not move (VT510, the page of each function). The attributes are in rect-attributes.vtt.

test DECERA acts on the rectangle
spec VT510 DECERA: CSI Pt ; Pl ; Pb ; Pr $ z erases the characters in the rectangle
known-fail: alacritty – no rectangular editing: DECERA, DECSERA, DECFRA and DECCRA are ignored
size 8 8
feed abcdefgh\r\nijklmnop\r\nqrstuvwx\r\nyz012345\r\nABCDEFGH\r\nIJKLMNOP\r\nQRSTUVWX\r\nYZ6789!@\e[5;5;7;7$z
screen
|abcdefgh|
|ijklmnop|
|qrstuvwx|
|yz012345|
|ABCD   H|
|IJKL   P|
|QRST   X|
|YZ6789!@|
test DECERA without an area takes the whole page
spec VT510 DECCARA, the area's parameters: Pt and Pl default to 1, Pb and Pr to the last line and column of the page
known-fail: alacritty – no rectangular editing: DECERA, DECSERA, DECFRA and DECCRA are ignored
size 8 8
feed abcdefgh\r\nijklmnop\r\nqrstuvwx\r\nyz012345\r\nABCDEFGH\r\nIJKLMNOP\r\nQRSTUVWX\r\nYZ6789!@\e[$z
screen
